      "name": "Move the graph into its repositories",
      "summary": "Creates the repositories, drains the open PRs until the source settles, seeds them, re-points the declaration and verifies a fresh clone, then has the parent consume the result additively, makes the first release and checks every identifier dereferences.",
      "description": "Creates the repositories, drains the open PRs until the source settles, seeds them, re-points the declaration and verifies a fresh clone, then has the parent consume the result additively, makes the first release and checks every identifier dereferences. Nothing is seeded on an unknown readiness, and a fresh clone that could not run is not a pass. Called by kg-separation and sub-kg-lifecycle (bpmn-authoring: split by phase).",
      "enforcement": "strict",
